IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 7 (industrial injuries benefits), Part I: unemployability supplement. The converter dropped the paragraph numbers; the eight
-- paragraphs follow the eight headings in the text: 1 Availability, 2 Rate and duration, 3 Increase of unemployability supplement,
-- 4 Increase for beneficiary's dependent children and qualifying young persons, 5 Additional provisions as to increase under paragraph 4,
-- 6 Increase for adult dependants, 7 Earnings to include occupational and personal pensions, 8 Dependency increases: continuation of awards.
-- (The text's own citations confirm 4, 5 and 6: "paragraph 5 below" in paragraph 4, "paragraph 4 above" in paragraph 5, "paragraph 4 or 6 above" in paragraphs 7 and 8.)
-- A reference such as "Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 5" is to the Schedule 4 amount, which the text omits (PLAN.md seam S34): it is taken as an input.
-- Ages are asked through the core's reading of "over" and "under" (s 173(a), seam K2) as `s 173(a) the person is under N` inputs.

§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- unemployability supplement`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- availability`

-- 1: "applies only in relation to persons who were beneficiaries in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act
-- immediately before 6th April 1987". A person who was not is outside the closed scope ("only"): FALSE. A person who was is inside the scope the sentence
-- states: TRUE (reading (e), NOTES.md: "only" is read as fixing the scope, as Part III paragraph 10(1) states its scope without the word; the other reading is
-- that "only" is a necessary condition and the answer inside is NOTHING). Whether a benefit is then payable is for the rest of the Part.
-- src:5383 | This Part of this Schedule applies only in relation to persons who were beneficiaries in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6th April 1987.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 1 (src:5383)
GIVEN `the person was in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 1 this Part applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6 April 1987`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- reading (e), mine: "applies only in relation to persons who were beneficiaries in receipt of unemployability supplement" is read as stating the Part's scope, so such a person is inside it
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only in relation to persons who were beneficiaries in receipt of unemployability supplement ... immediately before 6th April 1987"

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- rate and duration`

-- 2(3): a person "may be treated" as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently, though the loss of faculty does not prevent
-- capacity for work, if it is likely to prevent earnings in a year exceeding a prescribed amount "not less than £104". A prescribed amount
-- under £104 is outside the power, so the Act does not answer.
-- src:5387 | (3) For the purposes of this paragraph a person may be treated as being incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently, notwithstanding that the loss of faculty is not such as to prevent him being capable of work, if it is likely to prevent his earnings in a year exceeding a prescribed amount not less than £104.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 2(3) (src:5387)
GIVEN `the loss of faculty is likely to prevent the beneficiary's earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount prescribed in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 2(3) the beneficiary may be treated as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently` MEANS
    IF `the amount prescribed in pounds` LESS THAN 104
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a prescribed amount not less than £104"; a smaller amount is not one the text allows
    ELSE IF `the loss of faculty is likely to prevent the beneficiary's earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be treated ... if it is likely to prevent his earnings in a year exceeding a prescribed amount" (a failed "if")

-- 2(1): the weekly rate of a disablement pension "shall, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary is incapable of
-- work and likely to remain so permanently, be increased" by the Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 5 amount. Incapacity for work is the s 94(6)
-- answer (seam S36); a person treated under 2(3) counts as meeting it.
-- src:5385 | (1) The weekly rate of a disablement pension shall, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary is incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently, be increased by the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 5.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 2(1) (src:5385)
GIVEN `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary is likely to remain so permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary is treated as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 2(1) the weekly rate is increased` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the beneficiary is treated as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently under sub-paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the beneficiary is likely to remain so permanently`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... the beneficiary is incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently" (a failed "if")
        OTHERWISE `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do`   -- NOTHING when the s 94(6) answer is NOTHING

-- src:5385 | (1) The weekly rate of a disablement pension shall, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary is incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently, be increased by the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 5.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 2(1) (src:5385)
GIVEN `the weekly rate is increased` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt V para 5 the increase of the disablement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 2(1) the amount of the increase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the weekly rate is increased`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the increase is made is not answered
    WHEN JUST increased THEN
        IF increased
        THEN `sch 4 pt V para 5 the increase of the disablement pension in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
        ELSE JUST 0   -- no increase is made when the "if" fails

-- 2(2): the increase "is referred to in this Act as an 'unemployability supplement'": the name the core gives the benefit.
-- src:5386 | (2) An increase of pension under this paragraph is referred to in this Act as an “unemployability supplement”.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 2(2) (src:5386)
GIVETH A Benefit
`sch 7 pt I para 2(2) what an increase of pension under this paragraph is called` MEANS `unemployability supplement`

-- 2(4): an unemployability supplement "shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed
-- from time to time". It is payable on a day only within the period fixed at the grant or a renewal of it.
-- src:5388 | (4) An unemployability supplement shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 2(4) (src:5388)
GIVEN `the period determined when the supplement was granted` IS A Period
      `the periods for which it has been renewed` IS A LIST OF Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 2(4) the supplement is payable on the day` MEANS
    IF (day AT LEAST `the period determined when the supplement was granted`'s `the first day` AND day AT MOST `the period determined when the supplement was granted`'s `the last day`)
       OR any (GIVEN p YIELD day AT LEAST p's `the first day` AND day AT MOST p's `the last day`) `the periods for which it has been renewed`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable for such period" says when it MAY be payable; whether it is payable then is decided by the rest of the Act
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable for such period as may be determined" is a stated period; the sub-paragraph does not say the supplement is unpayable outside it

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- increase of unemployability supplement`

-- 3(1): if on the qualifying date the beneficiary was a man under 60 or a woman under 55, the weekly rate of the supplement "shall be
-- increased by the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 6". "Subject to the following provisions" (3(2) to (11)).
-- The age is asked as at the qualifying date (3(5) to (9)).
-- src:5390 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this paragraph, if on the qualifying date the beneficiary was—
-- src:5391 | (a) a man under the age of 60, or
-- src:5392 | (b) a woman under the age of 55,
-- src:5393 | the weekly rate of unemployability supplement shall be increased by the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 6.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(1) (src:5390-5393)
GIVEN sex IS A Sex
      `s 173(a) the person is under 60` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under 55` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 3(1) the beneficiary meets the age condition on the qualifying date` MEANS
    CONSIDER sex
    WHEN Man THEN `s 173(a) the person is under 60`
    WHEN Woman THEN `s 173(a) the person is under 55`

-- src:5390 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this paragraph, if on the qualifying date the beneficiary was—
-- src:5391 | (a) a man under the age of 60, or
-- src:5392 | (b) a woman under the age of 55,
-- src:5393 | the weekly rate of unemployability supplement shall be increased by the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 6.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(1) (src:5390-5393)
GIVEN `the beneficiary meets the age condition on the qualifying date` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt V para 6 the increase of the unemployability supplement in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 3(1) the increase before the deductions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the beneficiary meets the age condition on the qualifying date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the age answer is missing
    WHEN JUST met THEN
        IF met
        THEN `sch 4 pt V para 6 the increase of the unemployability supplement in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
        ELSE JUST 0   -- no increase is made when the "if" fails

-- 3(4), (3A) and (3): "additional pension" is the pension after any increase under section 52(3) but without any increase under paragraphs 1
-- and 2 of Schedule 5 (3(4)), and does not include any amount attributable to units of additional pension (3(3A)). "The relevant amount" is
-- that additional pension reduced by the amount of any reduction under section 46 of the Pensions Act (3(3)).
-- src:5395 | (3) In this paragraph “the relevant amount” means an amount equal to the additional pension reduced by the amount of any reduction in the weekly rate of the retirement ... made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act.
-- src:5396 | (3A) In sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) above references to additional pension do not include any amount of additional pension attributable to units of additional pension.
-- src:5398 | (4) In this paragraph references to an additional pension are references to that pension after any increase under section 52(3) above but without any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5 to this Act.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(3), (3A) and (4) (src:5395-5396) (src:5398)
GIVEN `the weekly additional pension after any increase under section 52(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it attributable to units of additional pension` IS A NUMBER
      `any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction in the weekly rate of the retirement pension made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 3(3) the relevant amount` MEANS
    max 0 (additional MINUS `the reduction in the weekly rate of the retirement pension made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act`)
    WHERE
        additional MEANS max 0 (`the weekly additional pension after any increase under section 52(3)` MINUS `the part of it attributable to units of additional pension` MINUS `any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5`)

-- 3(2): for a period in which the beneficiary is entitled to a Category A or B retirement pension whose rate includes an additional pension
-- mentioned in section 44(3)(b), the relevant amount is deducted from the increase; "an increase only if there is a balance ... and ... only to
-- an amount equal to it".
-- src:5394 | (2) Where for any period the beneficiary is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension ... and the weekly rate of the pension includes an additional pension such as is mentioned in section 44(3)(b) above, for that period the relevant amount shall be deducted from the amount that would otherwise be the increase under this paragraph and the beneficiary shall be entitled to an increase only if there is a balance after that deduction and, if there is such a balance, only to an amount equal to it.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(2) (src:5394)
GIVEN `the beneficiary is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the pension includes an additional pension such as is mentioned in section 44(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase that would otherwise be made under this paragraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 3(2) the increase after the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiary is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension for the period` AND `the weekly rate of the pension includes an additional pension such as is mentioned in section 44(3)(b)`
    THEN max 0 (`the increase that would otherwise be made under this paragraph` MINUS `the relevant amount`)   -- no balance, no increase
    ELSE `the increase that would otherwise be made under this paragraph`

-- 3(5), (6) and (7): the qualifying date. (5): the beginning of the first week for which the beneficiary qualified. (6): if the incapacity
-- forms part of a period of interruption of employment that has continued from an earlier date, the first day in that period which is a day
-- of incapacity for work, "or such earlier day as may be prescribed". (7), subject to (6): with two or more periods of entitlement, for a day
-- in one of them, the beginning of the first week of that period.
-- src:5399 | (5) In this paragraph “the qualifying date” means, subject to sub-paragraphs (6) and (7) below, the beginning of the first week for which the beneficiary qualified for unemployability supplement.
-- src:5400 | (6) If the incapacity for work in respect of which unemployability supplement is payable forms part of a period of interruption of employment which has continued from a date earlier than the date fixed under sub-paragraph (5) above, the qualifying date means the first day in that period which is a day of incapacity for work, or such earlier day as may be prescribed.
-- src:5401 | (7) Subject to sub-paragraph (6) above, if there have been two or more periods for which the beneficiary was entitled to unemployability supplement, the qualifying date shall be, in relation to unemployability supplement for a day in any one of those periods, the beginning of the first week of that period.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(5), (6) and (7) (src:5399-5401)
GIVEN `the beginning of the first week for which the beneficiary qualified for unemployability supplement` IS A DATE
      `the incapacity forms part of a period of interruption of employment which has continued from a date earlier than that beginning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day in that period which is a day of incapacity for work` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day prescribed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `there have been two or more periods for which the beneficiary was entitled to unemployability supplement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the first week of the period that includes the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 7 pt I para 3(5) the qualifying date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the incapacity forms part of a period of interruption of employment which has continued from a date earlier than that beginning`
            THEN CONSIDER `the earlier day prescribed`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN `the first day in that period which is a day of incapacity for work`
                 WHEN JUST prescribed THEN IF prescribed LESS THAN `the first day in that period which is a day of incapacity for work` THEN prescribed ELSE `the first day in that period which is a day of incapacity for work`
        IF `there have been two or more periods for which the beneficiary was entitled to unemployability supplement`
            THEN `the beginning of the first week of the period that includes the day`
        OTHERWISE `the beginning of the first week for which the beneficiary qualified for unemployability supplement`

-- 3(8) and (9): a break of more than 8 weeks in entitlement means the periods before and after are two different periods; a break of 8 weeks or
-- less is disregarded. The Secretary of State may by regulations substitute "a larger number of weeks" for 8: a regulation naming 8 or fewer
-- is outside the power.
-- src:5402 | (8) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (7) above—
-- src:5403 | (a) a break of more than 8 weeks in entitlement to unemployability supplement means that the periods before and after the break are two different periods; and
-- src:5404 | (b) a break of 8 weeks or less is to be disregarded.
-- src:5405 | (9) The Secretary of State may by regulations provide that sub-paragraph (8) above shall have effect as if for the references to 8 weeks there were substituted references to a larger number of weeks specified in the regulations.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(8) and (9) (src:5402-5405)
GIVEN `the break in entitlement, in weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks substituted for 8 by regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 3(8) the periods before and after the break are two different periods` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of weeks substituted for 8 by regulations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the break in entitlement, in weeks` GREATER THAN 8)
    WHEN JUST weeks THEN
        IF weeks GREATER THAN 8
        THEN JUST (`the break in entitlement, in weeks` GREATER THAN weeks)
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sub-paragraph (9) allows only "a larger number of weeks"

-- 3(10): "period of interruption of employment" has the same meaning as a jobseeking period, and any period linked to one, for the purposes of
-- the Jobseekers Act 1995. That Act is not among the sources, so the answer is taken as an input.
-- src:5406 | (10) In this paragraph “period of interruption of employment” has the same meaning as a jobseeking period and any period linked to such a period has for the purposes of the Jobseekers Act 1995.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(10) (src:5406)
GIVEN `the period is a jobseeking period, or a period linked to one, for the purposes of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 3(10) the period is a period of interruption of employment` MEANS
    `the period is a jobseeking period, or a period linked to one, for the purposes of the Jobseekers Act 1995`

-- 3(11): the paragraph is "subject to section 46(6) and (7)" (entitlement to guaranteed minimum pensions and increases of unemployability
-- supplement). Section 46(6) and (7) are not an answer this Part can read here, so whether they limit the increase is taken as an input;
-- when it does (or is unknown) the amount is not given.
-- src:5407 | (11) The provisions of this paragraph are subject to section 46(6) and (7) (entitlement to guaranteed minimum pensions and increases of unemployability supplement).
@ref sch 7 pt I para 3(11) (src:5407)
GIVEN `the increase under this paragraph` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `section 46(6) or (7) limits the increase` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 3(11) the increase subject to section 46(6) and (7)` MEANS
    IF `section 46(6) or (7) limits the increase` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN `the increase under this paragraph`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 46(6) and (7)"

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- increase for dependent children and qualifying young persons`

-- 4(6): "week" means "such period of 7 days as may be prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph": the core's sixth meaning.
-- src:5421 | (6) In this paragraph “week” means such period of 7 days as may be prescribed by regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 4(6) (src:5421)
GIVETH A `Week convention`
`sch 7 pt I para 4(6) the meaning of week` MEANS `such period of 7 days as may be prescribed`

-- 4(5): the Secretary of State may by order "substitute larger amounts for the amounts for the time being specified in sub-paragraph (4)".
-- The amount in force is the one the order names, and only a larger one is within the power.
-- src:5420 | (5) The Secretary of State may by order substitute larger amounts for the amounts for the time being specified in sub-paragraph (4) above.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 4(5) (src:5420)
GIVEN `the amount written in sub-paragraph (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount an order substitutes for it` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 4(5) the amount for the time being specified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount an order substitutes for it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the amount written in sub-paragraph (4)`
    WHEN JUST larger THEN
        IF larger GREATER THAN `the amount written in sub-paragraph (4)`
        THEN JUST larger
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the power is only to "substitute larger amounts"

-- 4(3) and (4): where the beneficiary is one of two persons who are spouses or civil partners residing together, or live together as if
-- married or civil partners, and the other had earnings in a week, then for the following week no increase is payable (a) for the first
-- child where the earnings were £215 or more and (b) for a further child for each complete £28 by which the earnings exceeded £215.
-- The result is how many of the children get no increase; the pounds are those "for the time being specified" (4(5)).
-- src:5411 | (3) In any case where—
-- src:5412 | (a) a beneficiary is one of two persons who are—
-- src:5413 | (i) spouses or civil partners residing together, or
-- src:5414 | (ii) two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners, and
-- src:5415 | (b) the other person had earnings in any week,
-- src:5416 | the beneficiary’s right to payment of increases for the following week under this paragraph shall be determined in accordance with sub-paragraph (4) below.
-- src:5417 | (4) No such increase shall be payable—
-- src:5418 | (a) in respect of the first child or qualifying young person where the earnings were £215 or more; and
-- src:5419 | (b) in respect of a further child or qualifying young person for each complete £28 by which the earnings exceeded £215.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 4(3) and (4) (src:5411-5419)
GIVEN `the beneficiary and the other person are spouses or civil partners residing together, or are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person had earnings in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of children and qualifying young persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds specified for the first child` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds specified for each further child` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 4(4) the number of children and qualifying young persons for whom no increase is payable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the beneficiary and the other person are spouses or civil partners residing together, or are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` AND `the other person had earnings in the week`)
       OR `the number of children and qualifying young persons` AT MOST 0
       OR `the earnings in pounds` LESS THAN `the pounds specified for the first child`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 1 PLUS min (`the number of children and qualifying young persons` MINUS 1) (FLOOR ((`the earnings in pounds` MINUS `the pounds specified for the first child`) DIVIDED BY `the pounds specified for each further child`))

-- 4(1): the weekly rate "shall be increased for any period during which the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit in respect of one or
-- more children or qualifying young persons", where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement, "subject to" 4 and 5.
-- 4(2): the amount is the Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 7 amount (omitted from this text).
-- src:5409 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and paragraph 5 below, the weekly rate of a disablement pension where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement shall be increased for any period during which the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit in respect of one or more children or qualifying young persons.
-- src:5410 | (2) The amount of the increase shall be as specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 7.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 4(1) and (2) (src:5409-5410)
GIVEN `the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit in respect of one or more children or qualifying young persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 4(1) the weekly rate is increased for children` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement" is a "where", not an "if", so the sentence says nothing of a beneficiary without one
        IF `the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit in respect of one or more children or qualifying young persons`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and paragraph 5"; the grant is cut back by 4(4) and 5(1)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be increased for any period during which the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit" (a failed "while": marginal reading (a))

-- src:5410 | (2) The amount of the increase shall be as specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 7.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 4(2) (src:5410)
GIVEN `the number of children and qualifying young persons for whom the increase is payable` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 7 the increase for each child or qualifying young person in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 4(2) the amount of the increase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 7 the increase for each child or qualifying young person in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
    WHEN JUST each THEN JUST (each TIMES `the number of children and qualifying young persons for whom the increase is payable`)

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- additional provisions as to the increase under paragraph 4`

-- 5(2): the condition in 5(1)(b) is treated as satisfied "if, and only if" (a) contributions are made at a weekly rate not less than the amount
-- referred to in that sub-paragraph (which refers to no amount), by the beneficiary or, for two spouses or civil partners residing together,
-- by them together, and (b) except in prescribed cases, they are over and above those required to satisfy section 143(1)(b) (seam S18).
-- src:5426 | (2) The condition specified in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) above is to be treated as satisfied if, and only if—
-- src:5427 | (a) such contributions are being made at a weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in that sub-paragraph—
-- src:5428 | (i) by the beneficiary, or
-- src:5429 | (ii) where the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together, by them together; and
-- src:5430 | (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above those required for the purposes of satisfying section 143(1)(b) above.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 5(2) (src:5426-5430)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the beneficiary` IS A NUMBER
      `the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the other spouse or civil partner` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `it is a prescribed case in which the contributions need not be over and above those required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 5(2) the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the amount referred to in that sub-paragraph"; sub-paragraph (1) refers to no amount
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        IF NOT rate AT LEAST amount
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if ... at a weekly rate not less than the amount"
        ELSE IF `it is a prescribed case in which the contributions need not be over and above those required`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)`
        WHERE
            rate MEANS IF `the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` THEN `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the beneficiary` PLUS `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the other spouse or civil partner` ELSE `the weekly rate of the contributions made by the beneficiary`

-- 5(1): an increase under paragraph 4 for a particular child "shall for any period be payable only if" (a) the beneficiary would be treated for
-- Part IX as having the child living with them, or (b) the requisite contributions are being made. "Only if" is a necessary condition.
-- src:5423 | (1) An increase under paragraph 4 above of any amount in respect of a particular child or qualifying young person shall for any period be payable only if during that period one or other of the following conditions is satisfied with respect to the child or qualifying young person—
-- src:5424 | (a) the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX of this Act as having the child or qualifying young person living with him; or
-- src:5425 | (b) the requisite contributions are being made to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 5(1) (src:5423-5425)
GIVEN `the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 5(1) the increase for the child may be payable` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable only if" is a necessary condition; paragraph 4 and the other conditions decide
    ELSE CONSIDER `the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): see 5(2)
         WHEN JUST satisfied THEN IF satisfied THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payable only if during that period one or other of the following conditions is satisfied"

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- increase for adult dependants`

-- 6(2): the requisite rate of contribution to the maintenance of a spouse or civil partner is "a weekly rate not less than" the Schedule 4 Part V
-- paragraph 8 amount.
-- src:5440 | (2) The amount of the increase under this paragraph shall be that specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 8 and the requisite rate for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(a) above is a weekly rate not less than that amount.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 6(2) (src:5440)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the beneficiary's contribution to the maintenance of their spouse or civil partner` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 8 the increase for an adult dependant in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 6(2) the beneficiary is contributing at the requisite rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 8 the increase for an adult dependant in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
    WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of the beneficiary's contribution to the maintenance of their spouse or civil partner` AT LEAST amount)

-- 6(1): where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement the weekly rate "shall be increased under this paragraph for any
-- period during which" (a) the beneficiary is residing with a spouse or civil partner or contributing to their maintenance at the requisite
-- rate, or (b) a person who is neither spouse nor civil partner nor a child or qualifying young person, and in relation to whom prescribed
-- further conditions are fulfilled, has the care of one or more children or qualifying young persons for whom the beneficiary is entitled to
-- child benefit. 6(3) to (6) let regulations remove or reduce the increase in earnings cases (inert, machinery).
-- src:5432 | (1) The weekly rate of a disablement pension where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement shall be increased under this paragraph for any period during which—
-- src:5433 | (a) the beneficiary is—
-- src:5434 | (i) residing with his spouse or civil partner, or
-- src:5435 | (ii) contributing to the maintenance of his spouse or civil partner at the requisite rate; or
-- src:5436 | (b) a person—
-- src:5437 | (i) who is neither the spouse or civil partner of the beneficiary nor a child or qualifying young person, and
-- src:5438 | (ii) in relation to whom such further conditions as may be prescribed are fulfilled,
-- src:5439 | has the care of one or more children or qualifying young persons in respect of whom the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 6(1) (src:5432-5439)
GIVEN `the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary is residing with their spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary is contributing to the maintenance of their spouse or civil partner at the requisite rate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a person who is neither the spouse or civil partner of the beneficiary nor a child or qualifying young person has the care of one or more children or qualifying young persons in respect of whom the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further conditions prescribed in relation to that person are fulfilled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 6(1) the weekly rate is increased for an adult dependant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the beneficiary is entitled to an unemployability supplement" is a "where", not an "if"
        IF `the beneficiary is residing with their spouse or civil partner`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the beneficiary is contributing to the maintenance of their spouse or civil partner at the requisite rate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a person who is neither the spouse or civil partner of the beneficiary nor a child or qualifying young person has the care of one or more children or qualifying young persons in respect of whom the beneficiary is entitled to child benefit` AND (`the further conditions prescribed in relation to that person are fulfilled` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the beneficiary is contributing to the maintenance of their spouse or civil partner at the requisite rate` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the further conditions prescribed in relation to that person are fulfilled` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on the Schedule 4 amount or on prescribed conditions that were not given
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be increased ... for any period during which" (a) or (b) (a failed "while": marginal reading (a))

-- 6(7): "A beneficiary shall not be entitled to an increase of benefit under this paragraph in respect of more than one person for the same period."
-- src:5450 | (7) A beneficiary shall not be entitled to an increase of benefit under this paragraph in respect of more than one person for the same period.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 6(7) (src:5450)
GIVEN `the number of persons in respect of whom the beneficiary would otherwise be entitled to an increase for the same period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 6(7) the number of persons in respect of whom the increase is payable` MEANS
    min 1 `the number of persons in respect of whom the beneficiary would otherwise be entitled to an increase for the same period`

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- earnings include occupational and personal pensions`

-- 7(1): "Except as may be prescribed, any reference to earnings in paragraph 4 or 6 above includes ... payments by way of occupational or personal pension."
-- 7(2): a power to make regulations about apportioning payments made otherwise than weekly (inert, machinery).
-- src:5452 | (1) Except as may be prescribed, any reference to earnings in paragraph 4 or 6 above includes a reference to payments by way of occupational or personal pension.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 7(1) (src:5452)
GIVEN `the earnings in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments by way of occupational or personal pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations prescribe that the pension payments are not included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 7 pt I para 7(1) the earnings counted for paragraph 4 or 6` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe that the pension payments are not included`
    THEN `the earnings in pounds`
    ELSE `the earnings in pounds` PLUS `the payments by way of occupational or personal pension in pounds`

§§ `Paragraph 8 -- dependency increases: continuation of awards in cases of fluctuating earnings`

-- 8(1) and (2): where a beneficiary was awarded an increase under paragraph 4 or 6 but ceases to be entitled by reason only that the weekly
-- earnings of another person (the relevant earner) exceed the amount of the increase or some specified amount, then, if and so long as the
-- beneficiary would have continued to be entitled disregarding the excess, the award continues in force but the increase is not payable for
-- any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed that amount. The relevant earnings are those that would be taken into account apart
-- from this paragraph (8(2)), which is the input.
-- src:5455 | (1) Where a beneficiary—
-- src:5456 | (a) has been awarded an increase of benefit under paragraph 4 or 6 above, but
-- src:5457 | (b) ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of some other person (“the relevant earner”) exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, some specified amount,
-- src:5458 | then, if and so long as the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding any such excess of earnings, the award shall continue in force but the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase or, as the case may be, the specified amount.
-- src:5459 | (2) In this paragraph the earnings which are relevant to any week are those earnings of the relevant earner which, apart from this paragraph, would be taken into account in determining whether the beneficiary is entitled to the increase in question for that week.
@ref sch 7 pt I para 8(1) and (2) (src:5455-5459)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has been awarded an increase of benefit under paragraph 4 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of the relevant earner exceed the amount of the increase or some specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding that excess of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings of the relevant earner which are relevant to the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the increase or the specified amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt I para 8(1) the increase is payable for the week` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the beneficiary has been awarded an increase of benefit under paragraph 4 or 6` AND `the beneficiary ceases to be entitled to the increase by reason only that the weekly earnings of the relevant earner exceed the amount of the increase or some specified amount` AND `the beneficiary would have continued to be entitled to the increase, disregarding that excess of earnings`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of a beneficiary who "has been awarded" an increase and "ceases to be entitled ... by reason only" of the earnings
    ELSE IF `the earnings of the relevant earner which are relevant to the week` GREATER THAN `the amount of the increase or the specified amount`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the increase shall not be payable for any week if the earnings relevant to that week exceed the amount of the increase"
         ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "the award shall continue in force"
